From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: the before-play pass puts the C and M rows of the list files first too (with EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_COMPUTE=1 / EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_MESH=1), and counts compute keys in done / total

Switches: none new. Acts in the before-play pass (EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_PREPASS=1, 0770) when
EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_COMPUTE=1 (0780/0781) or EDEN_UP_SHADER_SET_MESH=1 (0782/0783) is on. With
neither on, or without the prepass: nothing changes (no compute record is read, M and C rows are
counted as "not used" as 0770 counted them).

Why (T158 review, 13 Nov 2026): 0770's list pass took only the G rows of first_start.list. In d4
the start asked 458 graphics, 59 mesh and 94 compute pipelines; with 0780-0783 the set can hold
48 of those mesh and 87 of those compute pipelines, but they were prepared only in the whole-file
pass, in the file's order. A prepass cut short by its time limit could leave a quarter of what a
start needs.

What:
- ReadPrepassLists: M rows (EGPLIST1 kind 2) are taken as graphics keys when the mesh switch is
  on; C rows (EGPLIST1 kind 0, a 24-byte ComputePipelineCacheKey) when the compute switch is on,
  as the store's hash, KeptComputeHash = the C row's hash ^ "compute1" (the C row is
  ComputePipelineCacheKey::Hash(), as NoteFirstStartPipeline writes it). The report line names
  graphics, mesh and compute rows apart.
- ShaderSet::ReadRecords takes one more optional callback, compute_key_wanted: asked with a
  compute record's key bytes before its environment is built (as key_wanted for the others).
- The prepass's key count reads the compute records' keys too (keys only): every compute key not
  in the store goes into `left`, once. So done / total, the minutes left and the "N of M listed"
  numbers cover compute; mesh keys were in them already (a mesh key is a graphics key).
- PrepareShaderSet: in the prepass a compute record is read only when its key is still in `left`
  (and, in the list pass, named by a list), and is taken out of `left` then (each key built once,
  also with several jobs in flight); it is counted done when built or left out, and handed back
  to `left` when the pass stops before it is queued, as a graphics key is. 0781's skip of
  compute records in the list pass is gone: the list pass now takes the listed ones.
- The count line says how many of the records are compute.

Order of the prepass after this: listed G, M and C keys together (file order), then the records
of programs earlier sessions saw live, then the rest.

Needs 0770-0772 and 0780-0783. Checked: apply in name order on the core, PS5-target syntax check.
Not checked on the console.
